115	## #{#wsp2a authority=developer} Wealth Simple Format Validation
116	
117	**Description:**  
118	The validateFormat() method must verify that the CSV has the expected Wealth Simple column headers.
119	
120	**Authority Level:** developer  
121	**Priority:** High
122	
123	**Acceptance Criteria:**
124	
125	1. Method must check for presence of all required columns (case-insensitive)
126	2. Method must return true if all expected columns are present
127	3. Method must return false if any expected column is missing
128	4. Method must handle quoted column headers
129	5. Method must handle BOM in header row
130	6. Method must use inherited hasExpectedColumns() utility method
131	
132	**Implementation:**
133	
134	```typescript
135	validateFormat(csvContent: string): boolean {
136		const cleanContent = this.removeBOM(csvContent);
137		const rows = this.parseCSV(cleanContent);
138	
139		if (rows.length === 0) return false;
140	
141		const header = rows[0];
142		return this.hasExpectedColumns(header, this.EXPECTED_COLUMNS);
143	}
144	```
145	
