183	## #{#wsp2b authority=developer} Wealth Simple Transaction Parsing
184	
185	**Description:**  
186	The parse() method must extract transaction data from each row of the Wealth Simple CSV.
187	
188	**Authority Level:** developer  
189	**Priority:** High
190	
191	**Acceptance Criteria:**
192	
193	1. Method must skip the header row
194	2. Method must extract transaction_date from column index 0 (YYYY-MM-DD format)
195	3. Method must extract vendor_name from details column (index 3)
196	4. Method must extract amount from column index 4
197	5. Method must normalize amount (Wealth Simple uses positive for expenses, so invertSign=false)
198	6. Method must validate each field and report errors for invalid data
199	7. Method must continue parsing after errors, accumulating error messages
200	8. Method must return CSVParseResult with transactions array and errors array
201	
202	**Implementation:**
203	
204	```typescript
205	parse(csvContent: string): CSVParseResult {
206		const transactions: ParsedTransaction[] = [];
207		const errors: string[] = [];
208	
209		const cleanContent = this.removeBOM(csvContent);
210		const rows = this.parseCSV(cleanContent);
211	
212		// Skip header row
213		for (let i = 1; i < rows.length; i++) {
214			const row = rows[i];
215			const rowNumber = i + 1;
216	
217			// Skip empty rows
218			if (!row || row.every((cell) => !cell?.trim())) {
219				continue;
220			}
221	
222			// Validate row has enough columns
223			if (row.length < 5) {
224				errors.push(`Row ${rowNumber}: Incomplete row (expected 6 columns, got ${row.length})`);
225				continue;
226			}
227	
228			// Parse transaction_date (YYYY-MM-DD format)
229			const dateStr = row[0]?.trim();
230			const transactionDate = this.parseDate(dateStr);
231			if (!transactionDate) {
232				errors.push(`Row ${rowNumber}: Invalid transaction_date "${dateStr}"`);
233				continue;
234			}
235	
236			// Parse vendor_name from details column
237			const vendorName = row[3]?.trim();
238			if (!vendorName) {
239				errors.push(`Row ${rowNumber}: Missing details/vendor name`);
240				continue;
241			}
242	
243			// Parse amount
244			const amountStr = row[4]?.trim();
245			const rawAmount = this.parseAmount(amountStr);
246			if (rawAmount === null) {
247				errors.push(`Row ${rowNumber}: Invalid amount "${amountStr}"`);
248				continue;
249			}
250	
251			// Normalize amount (Wealth Simple uses positive for expenses, so don't invert)
252			const normalizedAmount = this.normalizeAmount(rawAmount, false);
253	
254			transactions.push({
255				transaction_date: transactionDate,
256				vendor_name: vendorName,
257				amount: normalizedAmount
258			});
259		}
260	
261		return { transactions, errors };
262	}
263	```
264	
